id who's come across  a book that can kill people is also an  immensely clever sociopath who relishes  the chance to use the death NART  and keeps its existence completely  secret for that very reason  Netflix's light is neither a genius nor  sociopath and only ends up becoming Kira  because he's pushed down the path of  darkness by other characters with the  genders of their own not because of the  dark aspects of his own character is  that what we're gonna do with the note  liked rules and warnings reuse purpose  to keep light as innocent as possible in  all this the filmmakers needed to shift  the blame for the plots death and  destruction on to someone else and Ryu  must have been a natural choice of  scapegoat White's girlfriend Muir  certainly plays her part in convincing  him to go crazy with the north but the  death God is painted as the true  instigator of the chaos which takes  place in the Netflix remake he's the one  who convinced his light to commit his  very first murder and he continues to  manipulate him from there on in in the  original Death Note  however reacts role is not to press a  lot into using the note but to simply  tag along  mostly because he's bored and finds  slights behavior interesting  a quick note at a hundred minutes when  God's film wasn't much longer than your  typical horror or comedy flick and  constituted far too short a time span to  do the detailed source material any kind  of justice these constraints meant that  certain vital plot points had to be  abandoned and relationships fast-tracked  the result being a movie that felt  completely rushed Death Note is not  light reading  after all there's a reason that Japanese  live-action version was split into two  separate films and even they had to skip  certain elements of the manga in the end  it might have served the Netflix version  better to have been produced as an  gentle series played out over ten hour  long episodes this problem with the  remake was best summed up in a review by  the LA Times shortly after death night's  debut it said for a film ten years in  the making that show up feels like  everyone involved is in a hurry to get  it over with  forcing love another character who  barely resembles the version on which  they were based is MIA who is turned  from an innocent bystander  into a genuine monster for the remake  when guards Death Note painter is  totally unhinged and entirely willing to  manipulate light into using the Death  Note without a second thought for the  repercussions  Netflix's Death Note also turned Mia and  light into some kind of tragic love  story when in the source material their  relationship was anything but  again this seems like an attempt to  shoehorn Hollywood storytelling  conventions into a story which only  succeeded by getting rid of them in the  first place in the real death narc the  only thing light ever falls in love with  is power
 

